Subject: [PATCH] net: sfp: refuse incomplete diagnostic data during hwmon probe

sfp_i2c_read() returns the completed byte count when an I2C transfer is
short. Only negative errors were rejected by sfp_hwmon_probe(), allowing
partially populated diagnostic calibration data to register a hwmon device.
Treat any incomplete read as EIO and use the existing bounded retry path.

--- a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
@@ -1723,7 +1723,9 @@ static void sfp_hwmon_probe(struct work_st
 	}
 
 	err = sfp_read(sfp, true, 0, &sfp->diag, sizeof(sfp->diag));
-	if (err < 0) {
+	if (err != sizeof(sfp->diag)) {
+		if (err >= 0)
+			err = -EIO;
 		if (sfp->hwmon_tries--) {
 			mod_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &sfp->hwmon_probe,
 					 T_PROBE_RETRY_SLOW);
